{"id": "EUVD-2026-95125", "enisaUuid": "ba2a4376-4329-3d5f-ac41-db38c0eef9ef", "description": "FFmpeg before 8.1.3 contains a protection mechanism failure in the HLS demuxer that allows attackers to bypass protocol and allowed_extensions restrictions when opening child playlists. Attackers can supply a crafted master playlist whose child playlists use disallowed protocols or non-multimedia local files, making parse_playlist() open resources the HLS security policy should block.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T17:30:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:05:52", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/23602df9cd1b485c45ba6f533d3b85569de3f323", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/01044d04536e", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/191715f0232c", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n8.1.2/libavformat/hls.c#L834", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ffmpeg-before-8.1.3-hls-demuxer-security-check-bypass-via-parse-playlist"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-107697", "GHSA-hhvh-2vr7-77mx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "93ea3596-eff1-334d-9365-3280bec63ef2", "product": {"name": "FFmpeg", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}, "product_version": "0 <8.1.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "340a5fed-6df6-3b05-b865-fbd8b64889b2", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}], "isExploited": false}